func=jag::game::InventoryManager::GetInventory	func_addr=0x00314af0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::InventoryManager::GetInventory(this, inventoryId, secondary) -> Inventory* (NULL if absent).\nSorted vector at this+0x8 (begin) / this+0x10 (end), element stride 0x48; key at element+0x0 is\n(inventoryId * 2 | secondary). Standard lower_bound; the returned pointer is element+0x8.\nEvidence: (1) identical key packing and identical 0x48-byte-stride lower_bound to Linux\njag::game::InventoryManager::GetInventory, returning element+0x8 the same way; (2) called with\nclient[0x19988] (the InventoryManager slot) from UpdateInvPartial, which falls back to\nCreateInventory on NULL exactly as Linux does; (3) same (this, u16 id, u8 flag) argument shape.
