func=jag::MiniMenu::RegisterComponentDoActions	func_addr=0x000e23d0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Second DoAction registration function (sibling of jag::MiniMenu::RegisterDoActions );\nboth are called back-to-back from jag::MiniMenu::MiniMenu , and those two calls are the\nONLY registration sites - so the complete DoAction set for this build is 7 here + 59 there \e 66.\n\nRegisters the interface-component family, which RegisterDoActions does not touch. Same object\nlayout: +0x00 callable vtable, +0x08 captured jag::Client*, +0x38 engaged ptr, +0x40 id, +0x44 kind.\nSender \e callable vtable +0x10.\n\n  action base  vtable   sender    id    kind\n  c69ff0       b597d8   01c190    1006  0     (sender sits outside the 0x10ad70-0x10bc30 band)\n  c6a110       b59748   10bc30    1005  0\n  c6a8b0       b59718   10bbf0      25  1     DoOpTargetComponent\n  c6a910       b597a8   10bbb0      30  1     DoOpDialog\n  c6a970       b59778   10bb70      57  1     DoOpComponent\n  c6a9c0    (copy c6a970) 10bb70   1007  1     DoOpComponent  - shares 57's callable\n  c69f80       b59688   10bb30      58  1     DoOpTargetComponentItem\n\nid 1007 copying id 57's callable is independently corroborated by the older Linux build, where\nCOMPONENT(57) and COMPONENT_SIXPLUS(1007) both resolve to the same address.
