func=jag::game::LinkMap::HasBridgeFlag	func_addr=0x003a6f30	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::LinkMap::HasBridgeFlag (Linux twin ). ReadTileFlags(this, mode\e1, tileX, tileY) then returns tile-settings bit 0x2 (BRIDGE / link-below) as bool; -1 (out of range) \e> false.\nMSVC also inlines this 3-instruction body at ~20 other sites (recognisable as `MOV EDX,1; CALL ReadTileFlags; CMP EAX,-1; JZ; TEST AL,2`), e.g. 0x36768a in FUN_00367640 (bridge-aware plane adjust, which reaches the LinkMap as World+0x140c8).
func=jag::MiniMenu::RegisterDoActions	func_addr=0x000e3300	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=DoAction registration. Signature: (retBuf, jag::Client* client). Installs one std::function-style\ncallable into each action object; param_2 (the Client) is the captured context.\nAction object \e 0x50 bytes: +0x00 callable vtable, +0x08 CAPTURED jag::Client*, +0x38 engaged\npointer (\e\e the object's own +0x00 when stored inline, which is always the case here),\n+0x40 actionId (static in .data), +0x44 kind (static in .data).\nCallable vtable is 0x30 bytes: +0x00/+0x08 dtor, +0x10 INVOKE (the sender), +0x18 clone,\n+0x20 destroy, +0x28 alloc helper. DoActionEntry dispatches through +0x10; the atexit thunk\nthrough +0x20.\nBecause +0x38 points back at +0x00, `this` at the sender call site IS the action object.\nThe senders are thin trampolines of the form\n    void sender(void* self, void* entrySharedPtr) { inner(*(Client**)(self + 8), protEntry, entry); }\nand they read ONLY self+0x8. Nothing else of `this` is touched.\naction base -> callable vtable -> sender RVA (61 entries, registration order):\n c69900 b59568 10b830 | c69950 b59358 10b5f0 | c699a0 b59208 10b3d0 | c699f0 b590b8 10b070\n c69a40 b58fc8 10b020 | c6aa10 b59658 10baf0 | c6aa80 b596e8 10bab0 | c6aae0 b595c8 10ba20\n c6ab40 b59598 10b9d0 | c6aba0 b59628 10b980 | c6ac00 b595f8 10b930 | c6ac60 b59508 10b8e0\n c6acc0 b594d8 10b890 | c6ad20 (copy c6ac60) 10b8e0 | c6ad80 (copy c6acc0) 10b890\n c6ade0 b59538 10b7e0 | c6ae50 b59448 10b790 | c6aea0 b59418 10b740 | c6af10 b594a8 10b6f0\n c6af80 b59478 10b6a0 | c6afd0 b59388 10b650 | c6b020 (copy c6ade0) 10b7e0\n c6b070 (copy c6ae50) 10b790 | c6b0d0 (copy c6aea0) 10b740 | c6b120 (copy c6af10) 10b6f0\n c6b170 (copy c6af80) 10b6a0 | c6b1c0 (copy c6afd0) 10b650 | c6b210 b593e8 10b5a0\n c6b260 b593b8 10b550 | c6b2b0 b592c8 10b500 | c6b300 b59298 10b4b0 | c6b350 b59328 10b460\n c6b3a0 b592f8 10b410 | c6b3f0 b591d8 10b380 | c6b440 b59268 10b330 | c6b490 b59238 10b2e0\n c6b4e0 b59148 10b290 | c6b530 b59118 10b240 | c6b580 b591a8 10b1f0 | c6b5d0 b59178 10b1a0\n c6b620 b59088 10b150 | c6b670 b59058 10b100 | c6b6c0 b590e8 10b0b0\n c6b710 (copy c6b3f0) 10b380 | c6b760 (copy c6b440) 10b330 | c6b7b0 (copy c6b490) 10b2e0\n c6b800 (copy c6b4e0) 10b290 | c6b850 (copy c6b530) 10b240 | c6b8a0 (copy c6b580) 10b1f0\n c6b8f0 (copy c6b5d0) 10b1a0 | c6b940 (copy c6b620) 10b150 | c6b990 (copy c6b670) 10b100\n c6b9e0 (copy c6b6c0) 10b0b0 | c6ba30 b58f98 10afb0 | c6ba80 b59028 10af40\n c6bad0 b58ff8 10aed0 | c6bb20 b58f08 10ae60 | c6bb70 b58ed8 10adf0 | c6bbc0 b596b8 10ba70\nKnown ids: c69900\e1/k3, c69950\e8/k4, c6afd0\e3003/k4, c6b3f0\e44/k7, c6b440\e45/k7,\nc6b6c0\e53/k7, c6b710\e2044/k7, c6b9e0\e2053/k7.\nThe nine "copy" entries at c6b710..c6b9e0 are the PLAYER +2000 block (2044..2053): each copies the\ncallable of its 44..53 counterpart, so the +2000 actions REUSE the same sender function.\nEvidence: (1) each action's atexit dtor thunk (e.g. FUN_007e4600 for c69900) reads the +0x38\npointer and calls vtable+0x20, comparing it against the object base - the std::function inline-SBO\ntest that proves +0x38 aliases +0x00; (2) the vtable installed here is the one DoActionEntry\ndispatches through at +0x10; (3) the .CRT$XCU initializer for each object only registers the\ndtor, so this function is the sole writer of +0x00/+0x08/+0x38.
func=jag::ClientProt::FlushMouseProtSender	func_addr=0x0014ba10	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::FlushMouseProtSender(MouseProtSenderBase *sender) -- generic per-tick driver shared by\nthe EVENT (aggregate+0x10) and NATIVE (aggregate+0x38) mouse senders. Called from\njag::ClientProt::FlushPerTick, EVENT first then NATIVE, once per game tick.\n\nTwo independent stages:\n\nSTAGE 1 (conditional) -- movement-history packet.\n  Gated on vtable slot 0 (HasPending): sender's CLICK ring non-empty OR\n  (clock 0x00e8e498 - sender->lastMoveSampleTime) > 0x7d0. So the history packet is emitted at most\n  every 0x7d0 clock units, or immediately whenever a click is also pending.\n  Loop: slot 4 (PopNativeMouseMoveSample) pops one sample and advances the move ring's read cursor;\n  x/y are clamped to 0..0xfffe with 0xffffffff meaning off-window; samples whose (x,y) equal\n  lastSentX/lastSentY are skipped without being written. Time is delta-encoded as\n  (sample->timestamp - lastMoveSampleTime) / 0x14 with the remainder accumulated and later emitted as\n  average + remainder bytes; the position uses a 1/2/4-byte tiered delta form. Each written sample also\n  calls vtable slot 5, which for the NATIVE sender is\n  jag::ClientProt::WriteNativeMouseMoveSourceByte -- one sample->sourceFlags byte per history sample.\n  The loop stops early when the packet approaches its size budget (slot 3 supplies the headroom).\n  A count byte is back-patched at the end.\n\nSTAGE 2 (unconditional) -- vtable slot 1 (SendEventMouseClick / SendNativeMouseClick) is tail-called\non EVERY invocation, including when HasPending was false. Each Send self-guards on its own click ring\nbeing non-empty, so per tick each sender emits at most one click packet.
