func=jag::EventListeners::CallListeners	func_addr=0x00786f30	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::EventListeners<std::function<bool(float,float)>>::CallListeners(inputHandler, x, y) -> bool.\nLocks the slot mutex at handler+0x290, walks the listener vector handler+0x278 (begin) ..\nhandler+0x280 (end), and for each non-null element invokes\n    callable \e *(void**)(*element + 0x38);\n    (*(code**)(*callable + 0x10))(callable, &x, &y);\nreturning 1 on the first listener that returns true, 0 if none consumed.\nNOTE the argument order is (&x, &y) - x first. Same std::function shape as the DoAction\ncallables: engaged pointer at +0x38, invoke at vtable slot 2 (+0x10).\nInputHandler listener-slot layout (derived, NOT the Linux 0x08 + n*0x40):\n    slot n at 0xd8 + n*0x68; within a slot: +0x00 begin, +0x08 end, +0x10 cap, +0x18 mutex.\n    slot 0  \e 0xd8  middle-button-down (walked inline by the WndProc dispatch)\n    slot 4  \e 0x278 mouse-motion (this function)\n    slot 17 \e 0x7c0 device-change (WM_DEVICECHANGE)\nEvidence: (1) identical iterate-and-stop-on-true contract to the Linux CallListeners;\n(2) the 0x68 slot stride is exact across all three observed slots ((0x278-0xd8)/0x68 \e 4,\n(0x7c0-0xd8)/0x68 \e 17) with the mutex consistently +0x18 inside the slot; (3) reached from\njag::input::Input::OnMouseMotion for every named handler and for the global handler.
