func=jag::graphics::GraphNode::UpdateBounds	func_addr=0x004c9530	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::graphics::GraphNode::UpdateBounds (Windows). MSVC outlined what GCC merged into the Linux\nflag-propagation walk  (branch at 0x788b30) - identical instruction-for-instruction:\n  TEST byte [node+0xfc],8            bounds-dirty flag\n  MOVUPS [node+0x40] <- [node+0x60]  transformed AABB min  <- source AABB min\n  MOVUPS [node+0x50] <- [node+0x70]  transformed AABB max  <- source AABB max\n  then GetWorldTransformationMatrixAligned + transform-in-place on node+0x40, and node+0x60 -> node+0x80\n\e> OGraphNode.BOUNDS_MIN_X/Z/Y \e 0x40/0x44/0x48 and BOUNDS_MAX_X/Z/Y \e 0x50/0x54/0x58, identical to Linux.\nThe GraphNode ctor  independently seeds 0x40/0x44/0x48 \e +FLT_MAX, 0x50/0x54/0x58 \e -FLT_MAX,\n0x5c \e -1.0f - byte-identical to the Linux ctor .
func=jag::Client::MainLogic	func_addr=0x00025870	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::Client::MainLogic(Client*, bool isLastTickOfFrame) - CERTAIN.\nPer-logic-tick entry, invoked from jag::GraphicsApp::Frame (0x00637670) via Client vtable slot\n+0xF0 as vt[+0xF0](this, i \e\e ticksThisFrame-1); the frame driver bumps clientCycle (+0x528) and\nrenderCycle (+0x530) around the call.\nEvidence (3 independent):\n 1. Call shape from the frame loop: (this, bool lastTick) - matches the 2-arg (client, byte) form\n    of the Linux jag::Client::MainLogic.\n 2. Head is a structural 1:1 with the Linux MainLogic head: leading "if (byte at high Client\n    offset) vt(this,0)", then a 5000 ms periodic process-memory poll, then a mutex-guarded bool\n    that early-outs into handler(connMgrLikeObj, clientCycle, renderCycle, lastTick).\n 3. That early-out call here is FUN_0010eaf0(client[0x198E0], *(int*)(client+0x528),\n    *(int*)(client+0x530), lastTick) - identical argument tuple to the Linux\n    LoginProtocolHandler(client[MAINLOGIC_MANAGER], clientCycle, renderCycle, lastTick).\nNote: the bulk of the tick body that GCC inlined into the Linux MainLogic stays outlined on MSVC\n(FUN_00025990 state query, FUN_00024fc0), so this function is far smaller than its Linux twin.
