func=jag::ClientStream::Write	func_addr=0x0063f5a0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientStream::Write(this, src, len) -> bytesWritten. Single funnel for ALL raw C->S bytes\n(already ISAAC-encrypted). Engine RawLoginDump hooks this for the raw login/RSA handshake.\nthis+0xe0 (byte) selects buffered mode: 0 \e immediate ws2_32 send(), non-0 \e append to the\npending vector (+0xc8 begin / +0xd0 end / +0xd8 cap) with grow-by-doubling, flushed by Flush.\nOn a short/failed send: Close + full ring reset.\nEvidence: (1) identical control flow and identical ClientStream field set to Linux\njag::ClientStream::Write; (2) calls ws2_32 send (Ordinal_19) + WSAGetLastError (Ordinal_111) where\nLinux calls send + __errno_location; (3) shares the bytes-written global _DAT_00e88a80 with Flush,\nexactly as the Linux pair shares its accumulator.
