func=jag::ClientVarDomain::SetVarValue	func_addr=0x00153fa0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientVarDomain::SetVarValue — string-truncating wrapper.\nApplies only when the var's type tag (varRef->[8]+0x48) is 2 and its element type\n(varRef->[8]+0x40)->[8] is the string type global DAT_00c88940; the value variant tag\n(value+0x18) must be 2 or the no-return failure helper fires.\nStrings of 0x50 (80) characters or fewer pass straight through; longer ones are re-encoded\ncharacter-by-character through the CP1252/UTF-8 lead-byte ladder and truncated at 80 CHARACTERS\n(not bytes), so multi-byte sequences are never split.\nNOTE: the 0x80/0x800/0xC0/0xE0/0x3F ladder constants live in the data globals\nDAT_00c695b1/b2/b4/b5/b6 rather than as instruction immediates — an immediate-based pattern scan\nfor this encoder will NOT find this function.\nBoth paths delegate to FUN_0011af00(this, varRef, value), which is the underlying setter and is\ndistinct from the three value-map setters FUN_00117e10 / FUN_00117f90 / FUN_00118130.
