func=jag::ClientProt::Construct	func_addr=0x0014a450	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::Construct(this, client) -- ctor of the ClientProt sender aggregate. Allocated 0x2870\nbytes and stored at client+0x19870, then pushed into the sender-provider list at client+0x19818.\n\nBase subobjects (each a MouseProtSenderBase-derived prot sender with vtable, client at +8,\nlastSentX/lastSentY at +0x10/+0x14, lastMoveSampleTime at +0x18, lastClickSampleTime at +0x20):\n  this+0x00  aggregate vtable 0x00b5a410\n  this+0x10  EVENT mouse sender, vtable 0x00b5a3e0 (slot0 EventMouseClickPending, slot1\n             SendEventMouseClick); its rings live on MainLogicManager, not here\n  this+0x38  NATIVE mouse sender, vtable 0x00b5a3b0 (slot0 NativeMouseClickPending, slot1\n             SendNativeMouseClick, slot2 prot descriptor, slot4 PopNativeMouseMoveSample,\n             slot5 WriteNativeMouseMoveSourceByte) -- type NativeMouseProt, owns both source rings\n\nRing initialisation proves the NativeMouseProt layout: the 10-iteration loop and the 200-iteration loop\nboth stride 0x30 and both zero sample+0x04..+0x13 and +0x28..+0x2f while seeding sample+0x20 \e 1;\nthe 8-byte stores at nativeProt+0x288 and +0x2810 zero each ring's write/read cursor pair.\n\nRegisters the NativeMouseProt's two listeners into the client's InputHandler (client+0x18E50):\n  clickListener (this+0x38+0x68) -> client+0x19678  (native-mouse-BUTTON listener vector, +0x828)\n  moveListener  (this+0x38+0x28) -> client+0x196e0  (native-mouse-MOVE   listener vector, +0x890)\nEach is a 0x40-byte eastl::function whose +0x38 self-pointer is what DispatchMouseEventWithSource\ndereferences before calling invoker slot +0x10. Torn down by\njag::ClientProt::DestroyNativeMouseProt.
