func=CreatePacket	func_addr=0x000af710	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=CreatePacket - outgoing TcpConnectionMessage factory.\n(shared_ptr<TcpConnectionMessage>* out, ProtEntry** prot, int* size, Isaac** isaac)\n\nWINDOWS TcpConnectionMessage field map (derived here + Init  + ReadIncomingMessage \n+ FlushClientMessages  + SendEventMouseClick  - five independent functions):\n  +0x00 protOpcode (u32)   -- Init writes prot->opcode; the low byte is the first payload byte\n  +0x04 protSize   (i32)   -- Init writes it; FUN_000e9540 reads it back as the handler's size arg\n  +0x10 buffer alloc base  -- Init's allocation triple; freed when the message is recycled\n  +0x18 buffer data ptr    -- every data[pos] write here and in SendEventMouseClick; the `src`\n                              argument of ClientStream::Write in FlushClientMessages\n  +0x20 write position     -- incremented per byte written; copied into +0x28 at enqueue time\n  +0x28 payload length     -- the `len` argument of ClientStream::Write\n  +0x38 ProtEntry back-ptr -- read by FUN_000e9540 as msg->prot, then prot+0x48 \e the handler\n\nPool: element stride 0x60; ref-count control block at elem+0x00 (vtable, strong +0x08, weak +0x0C),\nmessage object at elem+0x20. Same pool shape as the incoming factory in ReadIncomingMessage.\n\nServerConnection fields the inlined SendClientMessage tail uses: +0x48/+0x50 pending intrusive list,\n+0x58 freelist head, +0x60/+0x68 pool bump/end, +0x70 node stride, +0x88 pending count,\n+0x2b0 pending bytes, +0x40 outgoing Isaac* (the `isaac` this function receives).\nHYPOTHESIS: no official symbol (inlined on Linux) - do not rename.
