func=jag::ScriptRunner::ScriptRunner	func_addr=0x0008c460	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ScriptRunner ctor. Allocated 0x191ae8 bytes, stored at jag::Client + 0x19940.\nLayout: +0x00 vtable, +0x08 owner(Client), +0x10 int, +0x18 ptr,\n+0x20 \e ClientScriptState[32], stride 0xC850 (each slot: byte inUse at +0, state at +8),\nend of slot array \e +0x190A20 (verified by GetClientScriptState terminator).\nTail from +0x190A20: 8 EASTL vectors (2x 16-byte elem, 2x 0x178-byte elem \e CS2 hook context,\n2x 16-byte, 2x 0x18-byte) each reserved to 32, then an intrusive list + fields.
func=jag::input::Input::OnKeyCharInner	func_addr=0x00033e80	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=The `if (*(char *)(this + 0xc8) \e\e 0)` guard at the top is the Linux jag::input::Input::OnKeyChar\nwrapper (0x002e8990) inlined into the Inner: `if (this->consoleKeyHeld) return;`.\nSo Input+0xc8 is BOTH the engine's OInput.CONSOLE_KEY_HELD (Linux 0x98) and the field already\nrecorded as OInput.CONSOLE_OPEN_FLAG -- one and the same byte on Windows. It is set by\nOnKeyDownInner's 0x1ca3 path and cleared by OnKeyUpInner on vk 0x1ca3.\nWindows has no separate outer OnKeyChar; the vtable+0x18 slot points straight here.
