func=jag::MiniMenu::DoAction	func_addr=0x00167c80	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::MiniMenu::DoActionEntry(miniMenu, entry, screenXY). miniMenu+0x8 \e jag::Client*.\nOClient.MINIMENU \e 0x198e8.\naction \e *(entry->obj + 0x38); bails when action->[+0x38] is null.\nDISPATCH - DIFFERENT FROM LINUX:\n    callable \e *(void**)(action + 0x38);\n    (*(code**)(*callable + 0x10))(callable, entry);\ni.e. `this` is a SEPARATE CALLABLE OBJECT held at action+0x38, reached by a VIRTUAL call through\nits own vtable at offset 0x10 (slot 2), and arg2 is the entry - not the action, not the client,\nand not screenXY. Linux instead calls the raw function pointer at action+0x18 with the action\nitself as arg1. The engine's clientFakePtr shape does NOT port unchanged.\nAction object layout (0x50 bytes): +0x38 callable, +0x40 actionId, +0x44 kind.\nKind gate here: `(action->kind - 1) & 0xFFFFFFF7) \e\e 0` suppresses the click marker, matching the\nLinux `(kind & 0xFFFFFFF7) !\e 1` test on its +0x24 kind field.\nSpecial-cased action singletons: 00c6aa10 (checks entry->obj+0x48 \e\e 1), 00c6aa80, 00c6bbc0,\n00c69ff0, 00c6a8b0. Writes the click marker: kind at miniMenu+0x17c0 (1 or 2), x/y at\n+0x17c4/+0x17c8, +0x17cc \e 0; raw screenXY pair cached at miniMenu+0x17d0.\nTargeted entity: entry->obj+0x120 shared_ptr, notified via vtable +0xf8 with the client cycle.\nEvidence: (1) identical control flow, field set and five-way action-singleton comparison to Linux\njag::MiniMenu::DoActionEntry; (2) same entry+0x38 action / entry+0x120 targeted-entity offsets the\ncoordinator confirmed in MiniMenu::AddEntry; (3) same kind mask and same click-marker writes.
