func=jag::Client::ResetEntityManagers	func_addr=0x00027160	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Re-fires every entity manager's main-state-changed listener and detaches all per-entity\nscene attachments. Called from the region-rebuild paths (REBUILD_NORMAL, REBUILD_REGION)\nand from the scene-teardown wrapper FUN_00027740.\n\nFor SPOTANIM (Client+0x19948), PROJECTILE (+0x19920), ITEMSTACK (+0x198f8, +0x50\nsubobject), HINTTRAIL (+0x198b8), +0x198b0 and +0x19890 it invokes vtable slot +8 with\n(mainState, mainState) - the same listener slot jag::Client::SetMainState drives with\n(oldState, newState), and the same mainState int at Client+0x19f60. The overrides purge\nthe manager's collections.\nFor PLAYER_MANAGER (+0x19910) it walks the active-index int vector (+0x4038/+0x4040) into\nthe slot table (+0x10); for NPCList (+0x198f0) it walks the id array (+0xa0a0, count\n+0xb0a0) through jag::NPCList::GetNPCNode. Each entity is passed to an inplace-functor\n(vtables PTR_LAB_00b5e628 / PTR_LAB_00b5e6b8) that nulls and releases the attachment\nvectors at entity+0x1018/+0x1020 (and +0x1038/+0x1040 for players) and drops the\nshared_ptr at entity+0x48.\n\nFunction identity and behaviour are certain; the NAME is descriptive, not a recovered\nsymbol - the Linux counterpart FUN_00293200 (called from jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal\nimmediately before the store to [client+0x194b8]+0xc0e0) is unnamed there too.
