func=jag::game::AnimationSlot::ServiceLoad	func_addr=0x002f61c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Services one animation slot: resolves the pending seq through the type cache, builds its AnimationWrapper and swaps the pending pair into the active pair. The slot holds two 0x90-apart sub-slots; each is {id at +0x08, wrapper shared_ptr at +0x20 whose object word is +0x28}. The entity's primary slot is based at entity+0xa88, so its active id is 0xa90 and its wrapper shared_ptr base is 0xaa8 with the object at 0xab0.
func=jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::SetVarBitValueFromServer	func_addr=0x002eb320	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::setBitFromPacket(this, varBitInfo, value) - NOT ::setBit.\nReads the backing varp (varBitInfo->[+0x8]->[+0x40]->+0x8), lazily materialises it when the\nvariant tag is 4, then merges `value` into the bit range [varBitInfo+0x48 .. varBitInfo+0x4c]\nvia mask \e ((1 << (end - start + 1)) - 1) << start, and calls ::set(this, varBitInfo[+8]+0x38, &merged).\nEvidence: (1) the read-modify-write + delegate-to-set shape is unique to Linux\n::setBitFromPacket; Linux ::setBit does no bit merging at all; (2) identical +0x48/+0x4c bit-range\nfield pair and identical mask arithmetic; (3) identical `variant tag \e\e 4` lazy-init branch with\nthe same vtable call.
