func=jag::game::AnimationWrapper::Create	func_addr=0x002f92e0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=AnimationWrapper factory. Pool-allocates a 0x68-byte control block and publishes the wrapper at ctrl+0x20, so the caller receives {ctrl, obj}. Wrapper layout, identical to the ELF Create: +0x00 seq id (copied from animType+0x8), +0x08/+0x10 animation-type shared_ptr, +0x18 playback state, +0x20 flag byte, +0x24 frame cursor seeded to -1, +0x28 per-frame event std::function, +0x40 its invoker.
func=jag::ConnectionManager::ProcessConnections	func_addr=0x000e9c20	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ConnectionManager::ProcessConnections(ConnectionManager*, bool pumpInbound) - CERTAIN.\nStructural 1:1 with the Linux ProcessConnections: reads Client mainState (Client+0x19F60), branches\non 0x14 / 0x17 / 0x1E, calls TcpIn on the matching connection slot when pumpInbound is set,\nincrements a no-op-ping counter (+0x30 lobby / +0x4C game) and emits a keepalive message once it\npasses 0x32, then flushes; on failure runs the disconnect path (FUN_000e9430) and drops mainState\nvia SetMainState(client, 10) / SetMainState(client, 0x23).\nConnectionManager layout confirmed here: Client* @ +0x08, lobby slot @ +0x10 (connection ptr\n@ +0x18), game slot @ +0x20 (connection ptr @ +0x28), +0x30 / +0x4C ping counters, +0x38 deadline,\n+0x40 / +0x41 / +0x44 flags. Object is 0x58 bytes (allocation size at its construction site).\nThe ConnectionManager instance lives at Client+0x19878.
